KUF port M14: pipelines met during play are created without driver optimisation first
(VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_DISABLE_OPTIMIZATION_BIT), and an optimised replacement is built in the background. A draw that
needs a new pipeline waits for its creation at the end of the submission; with a cold pipeline cache this is the
longest stall in play (RADV, 2560x1440: median creation 27.7 -> 18.4 ms, 90th percentile 67 -> 38 ms; 0.1% low
18.2 -> 25.2 fps, longest frame 77 -> 60 ms). Replacements are built one at a time, only when no other creation is
queued, never on creation thread 0, and nothing waits for them; on failure the unoptimised pipeline stays. Only
with more than one creation thread. --vulkan_pipeline_fast_first_compile=false restores the old behaviour.
